{"severity":"error","file":"errors/int_overflow_1.march","start_line":5,"start_col":4,"end_line":5,"end_col":9,"message":"this addition may overflow Int in a `cap no_panic` module: nothing in scope keeps the result within [-2^62, 2^62) (e.g. n = 4611686018427387903).\n\nBound the operands with a refinement (`{v : Int | v < 1000000}`) or a guard (`if x < n do x + 1 ...`), or spell it `int_wrapping_add` if wrapping modulo 2^63 is what you want.","code":"int_overflow","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"REFINEMENT"}
